1
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:02,210
Bye-bye.

2
00:00:02,252 --> 00:00:04,546
I just got us
reservations at Michel's

3
00:00:04,588 --> 00:00:06,882
and tickets to The Music Man
to celebrate

4
00:00:06,924 --> 00:00:09,718
our first holiday season
as a be-troth-ed couple.

5
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:10,678
"Betrothed."

6
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:13,096
Betrothed couple.

7
00:00:13,138 --> 00:00:14,264
Hey.

8
00:00:14,306 --> 00:00:15,474
Hi.

9
00:00:15,516 --> 00:00:16,934
Ah...

10
00:00:16,976 --> 00:00:18,477
Oh...

11
00:00:21,772 --> 00:00:23,106
Pheebs?
Huh?

12
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:24,817
Skull?

13
00:00:24,859 --> 00:00:26,318
Oh, yeah, it's my mom's.

14
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,319
Oh, my God!

15
00:00:28,612 --> 00:00:30,948
No, no, no, it's not,
it's not my mom.

16
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:32,700
It belonged to my mom.

17
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:36,286
Yeah, no, she
used to put it out
every Christmas

18
00:00:36,328 --> 00:00:39,247
to remind us
that even though it's Christmas

19
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:41,458
people still die...

20
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:45,044
and, you can put
candy in it.

21
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:46,547
( giggles )

22
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:48,757
Hey.
Hey.

23
00:00:48,799 --> 00:00:49,967
Licorice?

24
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:52,469
Sure.

25
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,846
Hey, I just found out

26
00:00:53,888 --> 00:00:55,556
I get Ben
for the holidays this year.

27
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:56,891
Oh.
That's great.

28
00:00:56,932 --> 00:00:58,183
You going
to dress up as Santa?

29
00:00:58,225 --> 00:00:59,434
Nope.

30
00:00:59,476 --> 00:01:01,436
I mean,
I know Susan does every year

31
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:03,104
but I think I want
to take this year

32
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:04,690
to teach him all about Hanukkah.

33
00:01:04,732 --> 00:01:07,317
And maybe I could teach
Ben about the Christmas skull

34
00:01:07,359 --> 00:01:09,236
and how people die.

35
00:01:09,277 --> 00:01:12,531
You may need to use this year
to teach Ben about Phoebe.

36
00:01:12,573 --> 00:01:14,033
Hmm.

37
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:18,579
Hey.

38
00:01:24,043 --> 00:01:25,377
Did you know he was in there?

39
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:26,670
No.

40
00:01:28,129 --> 00:01:29,631
How long have we been home?

41
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:30,925
About a half an hour.

42
00:01:30,966 --> 00:01:32,426
Lovely.

43
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:44,605
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

44
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:47,024
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

45
00:01:47,066 --> 00:01:48,817
♪ Your love life's DOA ♪

46
00:01:48,859 --> 00:01:53,530
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

47
00:01:53,572 --> 00:01:56,825
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

48
00:01:56,867 --> 00:01:59,119
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

49
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:03,122
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

50
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:05,960
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

51
00:02:12,758 --> 00:02:14,259
Hey, you know
what I was thinking?

52
00:02:14,301 --> 00:02:16,303
When we get married,
are you going to, uh...

53
00:02:16,344 --> 00:02:17,721
Change your
last name to Bing?

54
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:20,557
No.

55
00:02:20,599 --> 00:02:23,018
Why not?

56
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:25,729
Bing's weird.

57
00:02:27,314 --> 00:02:28,523
Oh, hey, you guys.

58
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:29,524
Hi.

59
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:30,651
Can I have one to go?

60
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:31,652
Guess what?

61
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:33,070
My landlord just called

62
00:02:33,112 --> 00:02:35,114
and my apartment's going
to be ready soon

63
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,824
so I guess I'll be moving out.

64
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:38,700
Aw, Phoebe, I'm
going to miss you.

65
00:02:38,742 --> 00:02:40,786
Yes, you will be very sad.

66
00:02:40,828 --> 00:02:42,203
All right, well...

67
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:44,164
I got to go
tell Rachel the good news.

68
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:46,541
Oh, you guys going to be
living together again?

69
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:48,335
Yeah, why not?

70
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,004
Well, she's having
so much fun with Joey

71
00:02:50,045 --> 00:02:51,964
I just assumed she'd still
be living with him.

72
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:54,758
Why do you think she's having
so much fun living with Joey?

73
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:58,720
No reason except...
she... told me.

74
00:02:58,762 --> 00:03:00,347
Really?

75
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:02,975
So she said she didn't
want to live with me anymore?

76
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:04,893
No, no, she
didn't say that.

77
00:03:04,935 --> 00:03:07,562
I think you should
talk to Monica now.

78
00:03:07,604 --> 00:03:09,606
Phoebe, don't
worry about it.

79
00:03:09,648 --> 00:03:12,151
I'm sure she wants
to live with you.

80
00:03:12,191 --> 00:03:13,861
You're sure?
You're absolutely sure?

81
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:16,530
Well, no, but she
probably does.

82
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:17,572
Oh, probably?

83
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:19,366
Yeah, I don't like that word.

84
00:03:20,951 --> 00:03:23,037
Look, I know what
"probably" really means.

85
00:03:23,078 --> 00:03:24,872
Yeah, uh-huh, yeah.

86
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:27,332
Oh, your mom probably won't
kill herself, you know?

87
00:03:27,374 --> 00:03:28,876
Oh, you know

88
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:31,378
I'm sorry, but I'm not
hanging all my hopes

89
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:35,215
of Rachel and I living together
on-on-on "probably," you know?

90
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:38,301
You got to take care of yourself
in this world, you know?

91
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:39,845
If history teaches us nothing.

92
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:45,017
"Bing" doesn't seem
so weird now, does it?

93
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:50,064
( door opening )

94
00:03:50,105 --> 00:03:51,732
Hey, great, you're home.

95
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:53,775
Guess what Phoebe
got me for Christmas?

96
00:04:00,115 --> 00:04:02,409
( cymbal crash )

97
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:03,702
Drums?

98
00:04:03,744 --> 00:04:05,537
No, drums!

99
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,793
Hi.

100
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:14,171
Could we get two burritos
to go, please?

101
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:17,591
I'm sorry-- but
not that sorry

102
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:19,927
because you don't
have to live with it.

103
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:22,930
We have a reservation under
the name Chandler Bing.

104
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:26,516
Okay, we'll have a table for you
in about 45 minutes.

105
00:04:26,558 --> 00:04:28,018
45 minutes?

106
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:29,686
We have tickets
to The Music Man at 8:00.

107
00:04:29,728 --> 00:04:32,689
I'm sorry. Christmas
is a very busy time, sir.

108
00:04:32,731 --> 00:04:35,150
Is this because
of the burrito thing?

109
00:04:37,027 --> 00:04:39,113
You need to
give him money.

110
00:04:39,154 --> 00:04:40,989
Give him money?
It was a joke.

111
00:04:41,031 --> 00:04:42,323
No, to get a table.

112
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:44,910
Places like this are
always shaking you down.

113
00:04:44,952 --> 00:04:46,411
Everybody wants
a payoff.

114
00:04:46,453 --> 00:04:48,455
All right, calm down, O'Malley.

115
00:04:48,496 --> 00:04:51,959
I'll slip him some money.

116
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,294
All right, but you've got
to be smooth about it.

117
00:04:54,335 --> 00:04:56,171
Hey, I can be smooth.

118
00:05:00,092 --> 00:05:03,095
Listen, we're in
a little bit of a
hurry, so if you could

119
00:05:03,137 --> 00:05:05,305
get us a table a little
quicker, I'd appreciate it.

120
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:06,306
Of course, sir.

121
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:07,348
Okay.

122
00:05:09,226 --> 00:05:10,393
How'd it go?

123
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:12,687
Had the money
in the wrong hand.

124
00:05:16,817 --> 00:05:17,776
Whoo...

125
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:18,777
( laughing )

126
00:05:18,819 --> 00:05:19,987
Hey, you don't feel

127
00:05:20,028 --> 00:05:21,738
like you're going
to throw up, do you?

128
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:22,739
No.

129
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:26,076
Well, I do, so let's...

130
00:05:26,118 --> 00:05:27,828
So, Ben, you, uh...

131
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:31,999
you know what holiday
is coming up, don't you?

132
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,208
Christmas.

133
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:34,459
Yeah, and you know

134
00:05:34,501 --> 00:05:36,628
what other holiday
is coming up?

135
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:38,213
Christmas Eve.

136
00:05:39,214 --> 00:05:43,177
Yes, but also...?

137
00:05:43,218 --> 00:05:45,137
Hanukkah.

138
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:48,098
See, you're part Jewish

139
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:50,100
and-and Hanukkah
is a Jewish holiday.

140
00:05:50,142 --> 00:05:53,520
Santa has reindeers
that can fly.

141
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:54,980
Right, but on Hanukkah...

142
00:05:55,022 --> 00:05:57,024
Hanukkah's the
celebration
of a miracle.

143
00:05:57,065 --> 00:05:58,525
See, years and years ago

144
00:05:58,566 --> 00:06:01,111
there were these people
called the Maccabees.

145
00:06:01,153 --> 00:06:02,696
♪ Jingle bells,
jingle bells... ♪

146
00:06:02,737 --> 00:06:04,156
Okay.

147
00:06:04,198 --> 00:06:07,034
That's right, yes, but
on Hanukkah, we sing, uh...

148
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:10,704
♪ Dreidel, dreidel, dreidel,
I made you out of clay... ♪

149
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:13,414
♪ Rudolph
the red-nosed reindeer...♪

150
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:16,251
Okay, it's not a contest.

151
00:06:16,293 --> 00:06:18,128
When is Santa coming?

152
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:22,465
Well, how about this
year, instead of Santa

153
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:25,802
we have fun
celebrating Hanukkah?

154
00:06:25,844 --> 00:06:27,595
No Santa?

155
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:29,681
Was I bad?

156
00:06:29,723 --> 00:06:31,225
No. Oh, no, no. Hey.

157
00:06:31,266 --> 00:06:32,475
You weren't bad.

158
00:06:32,517 --> 00:06:34,561
You've been very good, Ben.

159
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:35,979
Santa's mad at me.

160
00:06:36,021 --> 00:06:37,438
Hey, hey. Come on.

161
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,858
Ben, Santa is not
mad at you, okay?

162
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:42,401
Hey, you're his
favorite little guy.

163
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:44,112
So Santa's coming?

164
00:06:45,989 --> 00:06:47,241
Yes.

165
00:06:47,282 --> 00:06:50,035
Santa's coming.

166
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:56,833
It's easy. Just
keep it casual.

167
00:06:56,875 --> 00:06:58,252
Give him a kind word

168
00:06:58,293 --> 00:07:00,419
shake his hand
and give him the money.

169
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:02,421
How do you know
so much about this?

170
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:03,757
I don't know.

171
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:06,927
Richard used to do it,
didn't he?

172
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:10,180
We'd be eating
our soup right now.

173
00:07:10,222 --> 00:07:12,849
Mustache bastard.

174
00:07:12,891 --> 00:07:14,268
Okay, those
people just left.

175
00:07:14,309 --> 00:07:16,061
Come on. Quick,
give him the money.

176
00:07:16,103 --> 00:07:17,271
We'll get their table.

177
00:07:18,272 --> 00:07:19,856
Excuse me.

178
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:27,614
We're in a bit
of a hurry.

179
00:07:27,655 --> 00:07:29,074
Certainly,
right this way.

180
00:07:29,116 --> 00:07:31,326
Ah, ha-ha-ha.

181
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:38,457
( drums and cymbals playing )

182
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:46,633
Ha!

183
00:07:46,674 --> 00:07:49,886
So you like the drums?

184
00:07:49,928 --> 00:07:52,347
That's... that's great.

185
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:57,227
You know, I was worried that
you know, they would create

186
00:07:57,269 --> 00:07:59,687
maybe an unbearable
living situation, but...

187
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:02,983
okay, well,
apparently not, so, yay!

188
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:04,484
Hey, hey, Pheebs,
check it out.

189
00:08:04,525 --> 00:08:06,153
We already learned
a song. Ready?

190
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:08,196
One, two,
three, four.

191
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:12,617
Tequila!
Tequila!

192
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:16,163
That's fun.

193
00:08:23,837 --> 00:08:25,297
Here you go.
Thank you, Gunther.

194
00:08:25,339 --> 00:08:26,465
Put her there.

195
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:29,176
( coins clanking )

196
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:32,471
Definitely not
easier with coins.

197
00:08:32,511 --> 00:08:34,055
Thank you.

198
00:08:34,097 --> 00:08:35,182
Thank you.

199
00:08:37,434 --> 00:08:38,726
Oh, hey, Pheebs.

200
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:39,936
Here.

201
00:08:39,978 --> 00:08:42,605
Now I only owe you $49.50.

202
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:43,731
Thanks.

203
00:08:43,773 --> 00:08:45,150
Hey.
Hey, Pheebs.

204
00:08:45,192 --> 00:08:46,901
If you want to get Joey
a Christmas present

205
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:48,945
that disrupts
the entire building

206
00:08:48,987 --> 00:08:52,115
why not get him something
a little bit more subtle

207
00:08:52,157 --> 00:08:54,868
like a wrecking ball
or a vial of small pox

208
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:56,453
to release
in the hallway?

209
00:08:56,495 --> 00:08:58,288
It's not just
the drum noise.

210
00:08:58,330 --> 00:08:59,789
Every five minutes

211
00:08:59,831 --> 00:09:01,958
Joey throws his sticks
in the air

212
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,085
and I have to hear,
"Oh, my eye!

213
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:05,586
Oh, God, my eye!"

214
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:07,255
I mean, it is so annoying.

215
00:09:07,297 --> 00:09:08,589
Yes, thank you.

216
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,967
You see,
this is how normal people

217
00:09:11,009 --> 00:09:13,178
are supposed to react to drums.

218
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:14,679
Wait a minute...

219
00:09:14,721 --> 00:09:16,764
Phoebe, you got Joey drums
to annoy Rachel

220
00:09:16,806 --> 00:09:18,892
so she wouldn't want
to live there anymore?

221
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:22,062
Maybe on some level.

222
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:30,862
Joey, you know

223
00:09:30,904 --> 00:09:32,072
that you could just not

224
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:33,781
throw the sticks
up in the air.

225
00:09:33,823 --> 00:09:35,992
What is rock 'n' roll
about that?

226
00:09:37,494 --> 00:09:38,619
Hey, Joey.

227
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:40,455
I got you another present.

228
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:43,708
Oh, wait, before you
tell me what it is...

229
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:46,461
( drum roll )

230
00:09:46,503 --> 00:09:48,129
( cymbals crash )

231
00:09:48,171 --> 00:09:49,881
Okay, what is it?

232
00:09:49,923 --> 00:09:52,884
It's a... tarantula!

233
00:09:55,554 --> 00:09:57,805
Oh...

234
00:09:57,847 --> 00:09:59,474
God.

235
00:09:59,516 --> 00:10:01,684
Rachel, what... I'm sorry.

236
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:03,353
What was I thinking

237
00:10:03,395 --> 00:10:06,523
giving Joey
this big, gross, scary spider

238
00:10:06,565 --> 00:10:09,317
in such a poorly
constructed cage?

239
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:11,236
What are you
talking about?

240
00:10:11,278 --> 00:10:12,612
I love them.

241
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:16,991
I had a tarantula
when I was a kid

242
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:19,660
but it died because my
cat ate it, and then...

243
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:23,790
then my cat died,
but, Joey, isn't this cool?

244
00:10:23,831 --> 00:10:24,791
Is it on me?

245
00:10:24,832 --> 00:10:26,000
I feel like it's on me.

246
00:10:26,042 --> 00:10:27,210
I got, I got...

247
00:10:29,379 --> 00:10:31,005
Oh, isn't that adorable?

248
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:33,300
Joey is afraid of the tarantula.

249
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:34,634
Oh, God.

250
00:10:34,675 --> 00:10:35,676
He's so adorable.

251
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:37,011
God, he's just
so much fun.

252
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:38,263
Joey's the best.

253
00:10:38,305 --> 00:10:40,474
I'm glad you're having
so much fun here.

254
00:10:40,515 --> 00:10:41,766
Whoa, wait, wait a minute.

255
00:10:41,808 --> 00:10:43,351
What...?
Phoebe, what's the matter?

256
00:10:43,393 --> 00:10:45,686
Our apartment is ready.

257
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:50,400
And that makes you angry
because...?

258
00:10:50,442 --> 00:10:53,278
Because you would rather
live here with Joey.

259
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:55,071
Where did you get that?

260
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:59,159
Monica and Chandler said that
you were having so much fun here

261
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:02,370
and apparently no amount
of drums or tarantulas

262
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:04,456
is going to change that.

263
00:11:04,498 --> 00:11:05,457
Phoebe...

264
00:11:05,499 --> 00:11:06,707
Hmm?

265
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:08,335
Did you get
all this stuff for Joey

266
00:11:08,376 --> 00:11:10,337
to try and drive me
out of the apartment?

267
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:12,130
Honey, if you wanted

268
00:11:12,172 --> 00:11:14,841
to do that, you might as well
just have gotten him a fish.

269
00:11:14,882 --> 00:11:16,426
You know how fish freak me out.

270
00:11:16,468 --> 00:11:18,219
Ah... fish.

271
00:11:18,261 --> 00:11:20,639
But it wouldn't

272
00:11:20,679 --> 00:11:22,056
have mattered anyway, Phoebe.

273
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:23,850
You and I are going
to live together.

274
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:25,519
We're roommates--
that's the deal.

275
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:28,021
Yes, but I wanted you
to want to live with me

276
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:30,940
but, okay, if you're having
so much fun over here...

277
00:11:30,982 --> 00:11:33,234
Oh, it's so much
more fun with you.

278
00:11:33,276 --> 00:11:34,402
We did have fun, didn't we?

279
00:11:34,444 --> 00:11:35,903
We did.
Yeah.

280
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:37,280
Well, anyway, they say

281
00:11:37,322 --> 00:11:39,533
if we want,
we could see it tonight.

282
00:11:39,574 --> 00:11:40,741
Oh, I would love to.

283
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:41,826
Yeah, okay.

284
00:11:41,868 --> 00:11:43,411
Oh, good, great.

285
00:11:43,453 --> 00:11:45,038
All right, good.

286
00:11:45,079 --> 00:11:47,999
Oh, and, Monica asked me
to make the drumming stop.

287
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:49,959
Um...

288
00:11:50,001 --> 00:11:51,002
Hmm...

289
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:54,005
Done.

290
00:12:00,761 --> 00:12:01,720
Hey.

291
00:12:01,762 --> 00:12:02,763
Hello, sir.

292
00:12:02,805 --> 00:12:04,307
You here to return
those pants?

293
00:12:10,647 --> 00:12:12,857
No, these are my pants.

294
00:12:12,899 --> 00:12:14,442
Oh.

295
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:16,695
Okay.

296
00:12:16,735 --> 00:12:17,987
How can I help you?

297
00:12:18,029 --> 00:12:20,448
Do you have a Santa outfit left?

298
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:21,782
Two days
before Christmas?

299
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:23,326
Sorry, man.

300
00:12:23,368 --> 00:12:27,080
Okay, look, do you have
anything, uh, Christmas-y?

301
00:12:27,121 --> 00:12:28,456
I promised my son

302
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:31,000
and I really don't want
to disappoint him.

303
00:12:31,042 --> 00:12:32,377
Um... come on...

304
00:12:32,419 --> 00:12:34,504
you got to have something.

305
00:12:34,546 --> 00:12:37,632
I'm the Holiday Armadillo!

306
00:12:40,343 --> 00:12:43,137
I'm a friend of Santa's

307
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:48,767
and he sent me here
to wish you a merry Christmas.

308
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:52,480
What happened to Santa,
Holiday Armadillo?

309
00:12:52,522 --> 00:12:59,654
Santa was unavailable
so close to Christmas.

310
00:12:59,696 --> 00:13:01,948
Oh, well, come in,
have a seat.

311
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:04,033
You must be exhausted
coming all the way from...

312
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:05,910
Texas.

313
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:09,997
Texas?

314
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:11,708
That's right, Ben.

315
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:17,380
I'm Santa's representative
for all the southern states

316
00:13:17,422 --> 00:13:20,925
and... Mexico!

317
00:13:20,967 --> 00:13:24,011
But Santa sent me here

318
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:27,641
to give you
these presents, Ben.

319
00:13:27,682 --> 00:13:30,893
Maybe the lady will help me
with these presents.

320
00:13:46,493 --> 00:13:47,952
Wow, thanks.

321
00:13:47,994 --> 00:13:49,454
You're welcome, Ben.

322
00:13:49,496 --> 00:13:51,539
Merry Christmas.

323
00:13:51,581 --> 00:13:57,295
Ooh, and Happy Hanukkah.

324
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:58,797
Are you for Hanukkah, too?

325
00:13:58,837 --> 00:14:00,757
Because I'm part Jewish.

326
00:14:00,799 --> 00:14:04,427
( gasps ):
You are? Me, too!

327
00:14:04,469 --> 00:14:08,431
Because armadillos also
wandered in the desert?

328
00:14:10,433 --> 00:14:13,353
You want to wander
in the hall?

329
00:14:14,979 --> 00:14:19,734
Hey, Ben, what if
the Holiday Armadillo

330
00:14:19,776 --> 00:14:23,404
told you all about
the Festival of Lights?

331
00:14:23,446 --> 00:14:25,072
Cool!

332
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:26,282
Come on, Ben.

333
00:14:29,494 --> 00:14:32,079
Years and years ago

334
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:36,209
there were these people
called the Maccabees.

335
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:40,213
Ho, ho, ho!
Merry Christmas.

336
00:14:41,589 --> 00:14:42,882
Santa!

337
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:44,342
Hey.

338
00:14:44,384 --> 00:14:48,137
What are you
doing here, Santa?

339
00:14:48,179 --> 00:14:52,933
Well, I'm here to see
my old buddy, Ben.

340
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:55,478
What are you doing here...

341
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:59,273
weird... turtle man?

342
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:03,277
I'm the Holiday Armadillo

343
00:15:03,319 --> 00:15:07,615
your part Jewish friend.

344
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,784
You sent me here

345
00:15:09,826 --> 00:15:15,122
to give Ben some
presents, remember?

346
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:17,375
What?

347
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:22,589
Did you bring me
any presents, Santa?

348
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:24,465
You bet I did, Ben.

349
00:15:24,507 --> 00:15:26,259
Put her there.

350
00:15:30,847 --> 00:15:32,724
Well, it would've worked
this time

351
00:15:32,766 --> 00:15:35,976
if his hands weren't
so damned small.

352
00:15:38,521 --> 00:15:41,900
Ho, ho, ho!

353
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:43,484
Ben, why don't you
open more presents

354
00:15:43,526 --> 00:15:44,736
and Santa,
the Armadillo and I

355
00:15:44,778 --> 00:15:46,320
will have a little talk
in the kitchen.

356
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:49,031
There's a sentence
I never thought I'd say.

357
00:15:51,242 --> 00:15:52,827
What are you doing?

358
00:15:52,869 --> 00:15:54,495
You called everyone and said

359
00:15:54,537 --> 00:15:56,955
you were having trouble
finding a Santa costume

360
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:58,917
so I borrowed one
from a guy at work.

361
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,628
Thank you,
but-but you got to leave.

362
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:03,296
Why?

363
00:16:03,337 --> 00:16:05,924
Because I'm finally getting him
excited about Hanukkah

364
00:16:05,964 --> 00:16:07,884
and you're wrecking it.

365
00:16:07,926 --> 00:16:09,761
But I didn't get
to shake my belly

366
00:16:09,803 --> 00:16:12,179
like a bowlful of jelly.

367
00:16:15,141 --> 00:16:16,559
I'm sorry, Chandler

368
00:16:16,601 --> 00:16:19,103
but this... this is
really important to me.

369
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:20,688
Okay, fine.

370
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:23,608
I'll give the suit back.

371
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:24,859
Hey.

372
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:27,153
You think you can
keep it another night?

373
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:31,783
Santa? Really?

374
00:16:31,825 --> 00:16:33,743
Yeah, is that okay?

375
00:16:33,785 --> 00:16:37,622
Did your dad ever
dress up like Santa?

376
00:16:37,664 --> 00:16:39,373
No.

377
00:16:39,415 --> 00:16:41,501
Then it's okay!

378
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:45,880
Okay, Ben,
Santa has to go.

379
00:16:45,922 --> 00:16:48,382
Say good-bye.

380
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:50,217
No, why does he have to go?

381
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:56,850
Because if Santa and
the Holiday... Armadillo...

382
00:16:58,810 --> 00:17:01,688
are ever in the same
room for too long

383
00:17:01,729 --> 00:17:05,817
the universe will implode.

384
00:17:05,859 --> 00:17:09,403
Merry Christmas!

385
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:12,156
No, why can't
the Armadillo leave?

386
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:13,908
I want Santa.

387
00:17:13,950 --> 00:17:17,411
Fine, I give up.

388
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:20,790
Santa, Santa can stay.

389
00:17:20,832 --> 00:17:22,792
Well, I'll stay

390
00:17:22,834 --> 00:17:27,505
but only because
I want to hear about Hanukkah.

391
00:17:27,547 --> 00:17:29,340
Ben

392
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:33,845
will you sit here with Santa
and learn about Hanukkah?

393
00:17:33,887 --> 00:17:35,972
Okay, Santa.

394
00:17:36,014 --> 00:17:37,181
( whispers ):
Thank you.

395
00:17:37,223 --> 00:17:38,307
You're welcome.

396
00:17:38,349 --> 00:17:39,559
All right...

397
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:43,813
it's time for the story
of Hanukkah.

398
00:17:43,855 --> 00:17:46,566
Years and years ago

399
00:17:46,607 --> 00:17:50,236
there were these people
called the Maccabees.

400
00:17:50,277 --> 00:17:52,906
Merry Christmas!

401
00:18:02,248 --> 00:18:04,291
Oh, wow.

402
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:05,501
Look at this place.

403
00:18:08,295 --> 00:18:10,590
Oh, this is terrible.

404
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:12,174
Oh, they've made so many changes

405
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:16,178
I can't even feel my
grandmother's presence anymore.

406
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:18,681
Ooh, new sconces.

407
00:18:18,723 --> 00:18:19,891
Oh, my God!

408
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:21,225
What?

409
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:23,477
Okay, remember, uh,
remember how you told me

410
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:25,479
that your grandmother
put up that wall

411
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:27,065
to make that
into two bedrooms?

412
00:18:27,147 --> 00:18:27,941
Yeah?

413
00:18:27,982 --> 00:18:28,942
And remember

414
00:18:28,983 --> 00:18:30,484
you said you were afraid

415
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:31,903
the landlord would find out
and tear it down?

416
00:18:31,945 --> 00:18:32,737
Yeah?

417
00:18:32,779 --> 00:18:34,113
Do you really not know

418
00:18:34,154 --> 00:18:35,782
where I'm going with this?

419
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:38,284
It left.

420
00:18:38,325 --> 00:18:39,619
It's one huge room.

421
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,412
Oh, no.

422
00:18:41,454 --> 00:18:42,663
( gasps )

423
00:18:42,705 --> 00:18:45,666
Wow!

424
00:18:45,708 --> 00:18:47,585
See?

425
00:18:47,627 --> 00:18:50,463
Well, I guess we'll just
have to put the wall back up.

426
00:18:50,504 --> 00:18:52,506
You can't,
because of the new skylight.

427
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:55,009
There's a skylight?

428
00:18:55,051 --> 00:18:57,386
Wow!

429
00:18:57,428 --> 00:18:58,805
Oh, so what should we do?

430
00:18:58,846 --> 00:19:01,139
Should we start looking
for a new place?

431
00:19:04,602 --> 00:19:08,022
You know, I'm sensing
that my grandmother

432
00:19:08,064 --> 00:19:10,190
would not be comfortable
with that.

433
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:12,860
Oh, yeah?

434
00:19:12,902 --> 00:19:16,114
Starting to feel her again
there, are we?

435
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:17,782
A little bit, yeah.

436
00:19:17,824 --> 00:19:19,158
Yeah...

437
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:21,828
Pheebs, is your
grandmother
maybe saying

438
00:19:21,869 --> 00:19:23,871
that you should
live here alone?

439
00:19:23,913 --> 00:19:26,332
You heard it, too?
You have the gift.

440
00:19:26,373 --> 00:19:29,669
Phoebe, it's okay.

441
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:32,296
I like living with Joey.

442
00:19:32,338 --> 00:19:33,965
Are you sure?

443
00:19:34,007 --> 00:19:36,634
Oh, please--
I hate packing,
it's closer to work

444
00:19:36,676 --> 00:19:39,553
and we do have fun.

445
00:19:39,595 --> 00:19:43,516
Although, I'm really going
to miss living with you.

446
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:44,851
Oh, me, too.

447
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:46,811
I know.

448
00:19:46,853 --> 00:19:49,730
Oh, oh, wait, did you
hear that? Listen...

449
00:19:49,772 --> 00:19:52,191
Huh?
I'm getting something
from your grandmother.

450
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:53,484
She said that since

451
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:55,862
you get to keep the
one-bedroom apartment

452
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:59,323
you should give Rachel
the purple chair?

453
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:03,786
No, I do not hear that.

454
00:20:05,538 --> 00:20:08,666
And the miracle was that
that little bit of oil

455
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:11,085
that should have
lasted just one day

456
00:20:11,127 --> 00:20:12,712
burned for...

457
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:13,838
Eight whole days.

458
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:15,048
That's right.

459
00:20:15,089 --> 00:20:17,175
And that's why we
celebrate Hanukkah.

460
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,801
The end.

461
00:20:18,843 --> 00:20:21,303
Awesome.

462
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:23,639
My favorite part
was when Superman

463
00:20:23,681 --> 00:20:27,018
flew all the Jews
out of Egypt.

464
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:32,690
The armadillo
was actually

465
00:20:32,732 --> 00:20:35,026
not so thrilled
about that part.

466
00:20:36,569 --> 00:20:37,778
Okay, Ben

467
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:42,449
it's time to light
the Hanukkah candles!

468
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:44,160
Oh, ho, ho.

469
00:20:50,457 --> 00:20:52,418
Hey...

470
00:20:52,459 --> 00:20:53,878
Oh, wow.

471
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:56,505
Looks like the Easter
Bunny's funeral in here.

472
00:20:59,175 --> 00:21:01,301
Come on, come on,
we're lighting the candles.

473
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:02,636
Come on.

474
00:21:02,678 --> 00:21:04,013
Oh.
Oh.

475
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:09,018
Okay, I understand
why Superman is here

476
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:12,855
but why is there a porcupine
at the Easter Bunny's funeral?

477
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:21,488
Joey:
Did you get it?

478
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:22,531
I got it.

479
00:21:22,573 --> 00:21:24,658
Is it back in the cage?

480
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:27,828
It's back in the cage.

481
00:21:27,870 --> 00:21:29,872
Is the cage closed?

482
00:21:29,914 --> 00:21:33,375
Joey, will you just
come out here

483
00:21:33,417 --> 00:21:34,877
and stop being such a baby?!

484
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:44,720
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

